### Feature Session — las tres modalidades
### OPEN: login, refresh, logout · JWT: perfil y permisos · JWT + RBAC: el resto de la API
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@access = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.$.refresh_token}}

### ===================== OPEN =====================

### LOGIN -> 200 (caja). Guarda access_token y refresh_token.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "Jaider",
  "password": "23456789"
}

### 401 — contraseña incorrecta (mismo mensaje que usuario inexistente)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "caja",
  "password": "otra"
}

### LOGIN con el correo en lugar del username -> 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "caja@tazanorte.local",
  "password": "Caja123!"
}

### ===================== JWT =====================

### PERFIL
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/perfil
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### MIS PERMISOS (los 30 de CAJA)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/permisos
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### 401 — perfil sin token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/perfil

### ===================== JWT + RBAC =====================

### 200 — CAJA puede listar pedidos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### 403 — CAJA no administra usuarios
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### ===================== REFRESH Y REUSO =====================

### REFRESH -> 200: par nuevo; el refresh anterior queda inválido
# @name renovar
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}"
}

### 401 — REUSO: presentar otra vez el refresh ya usado revoca toda la familia
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}"
}

### 401 — el refresh nuevo también murió (la familia fue revocada)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{renovar.response.body.$.refresh_token}}"
}

### ===================== LOGOUT =====================

### Nuevo login para probar el cierre de sesión
# @name login2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "caja",
  "password": "Caja123!"
}

### LOGOUT -> 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{login2.response.body.$.refresh_token}}"
}

### 401 — ese refresh ya no renueva
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{login2.response.body.$.refresh_token}}"
}
